1
00:03:46,153 --> 00:03:52,153
They only met once, but it changed their lives forever.

2
00:07:32,307 --> 00:07:38,307
The Breakfast Club is a comedy, drama film directed by John Hughes.

3
00:11:18,461 --> 00:11:24,461
Five high school students from different walks of life endure a
Saturday detention under a power-hungry principal.

4
00:15:04,615 --> 00:15:10,615
The disparate group includes rebel John, princess Claire,
outcast Allison, brainy Brian and Andrew, the jock.

5
00:18:50,769 --> 00:18:56,769
Each has a chance to tell his or her story, making the others see them a little differently
-- and when the day ends, they question whether school will ever be the same.

6
00:22:36,923 --> 00:22:42,923
Andrew Clark, played by Emilio Estevez.

7
00:26:23,076 --> 00:26:29,076
John Bender, played by Judd Nelson.

8
00:30:09,230 --> 00:30:15,230
Claire Standish, played by Molly Ringwald.

9
00:33:55,384 --> 00:34:01,384
Brian Johnson, played by Anthony Michael Hall.

10
00:37:41,538 --> 00:37:47,538
Allison Reynolds, played by Ally Sheedy.

11
00:41:27,692 --> 00:41:33,692
Richard Vernon, played by Paul Gleason.

12
00:45:13,846 --> 00:45:19,846
The Breakfast Club is a 1985 American coming-of-age comedy-drama
film written, produced, and directed by John Hughes.

13
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
It stars Emilio Estevez, Paul Gleason, Anthony Michael Hall,
Judd Nelson, Molly Ringwald, and Ally Sheedy.

14
00:52:46,153 --> 00:52:52,153
The film tells the story of five teenagers from different high school cliques who serve
a Saturday detention overseen by their authoritarian Vice Principal.

15
00:56:32,307 --> 00:56:38,307
Hughes had written the script in 1982, and began casting for the
film after the release of Sixteen Candles (1984).

16
01:00:18,461 --> 01:00:24,461
Filming took place from March to May 1984, and the entire film was shot
at Maine North High School in Des Plaines, Illinois.

17
01:04:04,615 --> 01:04:10,615
Although the film is technically not an independent film due to Universal Pictures' involvement as a producer, The Breakfast Club has been popularly recognized
as one; the low budget, Universal not being the primary production company, and the overall feel of the film are factors to its recognition.

18
01:07:50,769 --> 01:07:56,769
The film premiered in Los Angeles on February 7, 1985, and was
theatrically released by Universal Pictures on February 15, 1985.

19
01:11:36,923 --> 01:11:42,923
It grossed $51.5 million against a $1 million budget, and earned acclaim from critics,
who consider it to be one of Hughes's most memorable and recognized works.

20
01:15:23,076 --> 01:15:29,076
The media subsequently referred to the film's five main actors
as members of a group called the "Brat Pack".

21
01:19:09,230 --> 01:19:15,230
In 2015, the film was digitally remastered and was re-screened in
430 theaters in celebration of its 30th anniversary.

22
01:22:55,384 --> 01:23:01,384
In 2016, The Breakfast Club was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by
the Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

23
01:26:41,538 --> 01:26:47,538
The film has been considered as one of the best films of the
1980s, and one of the best teen films of all time.

24
01:30:27,692 --> 01:30:33,692
The film explores themes of high school, coming of age,
teen angst, detention, teenage rebellion.

25
01:34:13,846 --> 01:34:19,846
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
